{
  "account": "plur",
  "background": { "color": "#0A0A0A" },
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "main": "WAREHOUSE PARTY",
      "sub": "The illegal aesthetic — 40,000 people danced on a forbidden night."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1989. London.",
        "You never knew where you'd dance",
        "until the night before.",
        "The address was never posted in advance."
      ],
      "sub": "The night was always a secret."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "You called a number.",
        "A recorded message played:",
        "\"Head north on the M25.",
        "Exit at junction 8.",
        "Turn left when you see the sign.\""
      ],
      "sub": "The motorway was the venue."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Abandoned factories.",
        "Derelict warehouses. Old hospitals.",
        "Speakers reaching the ceiling.",
        "5,000. 10,000. 25,000 people."
      ],
      "sub": "The spaces no one wanted became the places everyone needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Tony Colston-Hayter. 22 years old.",
        "He named the parties Sunrise.",
        "There was a loophole:",
        "call it members only —",
        "and legally you were safe."
      ],
      "sub": "For a while."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "22 May 1992.",
        "Castlemorton Common.",
        "Spiral Tribe. DiY Sound System. Bedlam.",
        "One week. 40,000 people.",
        "It never stopped."
      ],
      "sub": "The government was watching."
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "quote": [
        "Music characterised by",
        "the emission of a succession",
        "of repetitive beats."
      ],
      "note": "Criminal Justice Act, 1994 — the legal definition of rave music, now a criminal offence"
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "No one was thinking about the law.",
        "They were just dancing."
      ],
      "strobe": "Castlemorton 1992",
      "cta": "Save this. You'll want to read it again."
    }
  ]
}
